  "measurement": "Fresh process/tree per run, serialized on CPU4; alternate before/current order each repeat; report medians of5. Timed loops include allocation and checksum, excluding trace generation, construction, reservation, verification and output. No compile/test/other benchmark ran concurrently.",
  "memory": "Process peak RSS captured before independent reference verification, including input traces, tree storage and transient vector reallocation. Search also holds its preparation trace and probe trace; 128-bit search additionally holds a separate vector of 500000 128-bit thresholds.",
  "variants": {
    "before_refinement": "Published endpoint/alignment version before the continued optimization loop; sources snapshotted under /tmp/segment-pool-before",
    "current": "Workspace checkpoint: ordinary positionless leaves; lazy moved construction, nontrivial-action borrowing, optional cached branch bit, and smaller field order for applicable generic types; ordinary/Init set consumes its owned input value at the leaf"
  },
  "validation": "O2 warning builds and ASan+UBSan passed common randomized/structural, generic ownership/non-default-construction/throwing-predicate, dense/naive utility parity,128-bit coordinate/count/aggregate and two-TU utility checks. Alternative branch layouts were separately checked for alignment, final size, copy/move/clear/reserve, updates and searches. Generic-layout default64/128 benchmark .text matches copy_bitcache exactly. First repeat of each final condition verified against independent references after timing; all repeats agree in checksums and node counts. Leak detection disabled due ptrace environment.",
  "changes": [
    "Remove ordinary leaf positions and recover them from the descent bounds; scalar leaves16->8B, branches remain32B",
    "Move newly computed lazy leaf/branch values and avoid unnecessary old-value copies during splitting",
    "Borrow nontrivial parent actions during propagation; retain cheap local copies for trivial actions",
    "Cache immutable branch-bit positions only when the added byte fits existing tail padding",
    "Select F-first or Index-first lazy branch layouts only when strictly smaller; ties retain the existing layout",
    "Match all13 dense ordinary utility families, with uniform Init aliases, and all13 dense lazy utility families; coordinate/count fields use Index",
    "Represent arithmetic-progression sums as an affine expression of the query origin, so huge-N uniform initialization needs no per-point setup",
    "Consume ordinary/Init point-update values at the leaf to remove one internal copy per set; tested scalar benchmark .text is unchanged"
  ],
  "tradeoffs": "Small timing regressions are retained in time_regressions. Ordinary initialized-node bytes and vector element sizes shrink, but local peak RSS can rise around1MiB; allocator retention is a plausible explanation, not a proven attribution. Most rejected candidates reduced one local cost while slowing other workloads. Generic layout choices reduce padding for applicable types; no speed claim is made for those unbenchmarked generic configurations.",
